 what I find useful is  having very specific numbers and tasks  so for example in my Arabic where I  sometimes feel that I'm treading water  and not progressing as quickly as I  would like I make sure that every day I  review three of the many stories in  linked stories that I have already gone  through and of course forgot the most  the words that I looked up but I'll go  through three of them at least a day and  I'll do it while listening to the  natural voice and typically you know you  can reset it five seconds so five  seconds and I do it by the way in  sentence view so that five seconds of  the voice corresponds more or less of  the narrator's course to to a sentence  and so I go through three of these a day  that's I have to do that that's a  specific task that I set myself of  course I always listen when I have an  opportunity while in the car doing  dishes going for a walk and so forth I  have observed that because on the  playlist it records how many times  you've listened to these stories and of  course I have listened to the earlier  stories more often than the later  stories and I find that those stories  that I know the best are the ones that I  have listened to at least thirty times  in fact there are even some later  stories that I have listened to more  often and I understand those better so I  know again a very specific mechanical  thing I have to listen at least thirty  times before these stories are gonna  soak in as meaning without me having to  translate other sort of objective  numbers that I'm aware of the goals that  I have to reach I know from experience  that until I have three thousand known  words that we recount them at length I  won't be able to have much of a  conversation with anyone so I'm at 800  known words in Arabic so I'm gonna have  to wait until I reach 3,000 before I  have a discussion with anyone just let  the phone ring so these are some of the  specific number tasks  modern yeah all right  so specific tasks specific milestones  are very useful I know from experience  that when I have thirty thousand known  words I will and not until will I be  able to kind of read newspapers  understand sort of news broadcast things  of that nature I may not be able to but  before that is highly unlikely that I'll  be able to now people will say that the  known words total it means different  things in different languages and  there's so many variations of the words  in Arabic you know they tack on the end  what to the beginning of a word so every  word if you say an a car that's another  word so you know these numbers are not  scientific  you know statistics on how many words  you know but it's an indicator and I  find all of these numerical indicators  that we have a link are very helpful in  terms of guiding us through the sort of  daily tasks shorter term goals and our  ability to follow our progress towards  these shorter term goals that keep us  motivated when even though we have a  long-term goal of wanting to learn a  certain language our motivation Flags in  the short-term and so that's you know my  advice on dealing with short-term  motivation thank you for listening and  Daniel please contact us and so that we  can set up the meeting  thank you bye for now  [Music]
 

